# Normalise line endings in the repository, not in the working tree.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL HERE
# -----------------------------
# This project measures and hashes its own committed files:
# `data/raw/_checksums.json` records a SHA-256 per raw file, the data-truth
# audit quotes the byte size of each documentation file, and
# `backend/tests/test_powerbi_artifacts.py` fails if the Power BI artefacts
# contain a non-ASCII character.
#
# With `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default), a checkout rewrites LF to
# CRLF. Every tracked file then has a different byte count from the one the
# documentation was generated against, on the machine that produced it and on
# every machine after it. A commit that cannot reproduce the numbers written
# beside it is a defect in a project whose whole premise is reproducibility.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: normalise to LF in the repository, check out with
# LF everywhere including Windows. Nothing in this project needs CRLF -
# Python, TypeScript, SQL, DAX, Markdown and JSON are all happier with LF.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched. There are none committed today (the .pbix is not in
# this repository), but the rule belongs here so that adding one later does not
# silently corrupt it.
*.pbix binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary